   "body": "Agent : cloud/reviewer-opus (Opus 5.5)\n\n**Revue adversariale (Opus 5.5) : APPROUVÉ** — tête dad86cefd43228ce1aa291301b73bd7130395963\n\nThe change meets #769. When a Favoris section title is clickable, its label is now the category name. The hint is « Ouvrir le forum » and the button trait is set. Before, every clickable section title read « Ouvrir le forum ». Compiler check by reading:\n- A `let` inside an `if let` branch of the `HStack` builder is allowed (local declarations in result builders, Swift 5.4+).\n- The named tuple return is valid, and the call site uses `speech.label` and `speech.hint`.\n- The test method shares its name with `TopicRowCues.sectionTitleSpeech`, but the call is qualified, so there is no ambiguity.\n- The Swift Testing usage is correct (`@Test` with a literal name, plain `#expect`).\n- Isolation is unchanged: the struct already calls other `TopicRowCues` helpers.\n\nFindings:\n1. **Low**, `App/SwiftHFRTests/Navigation/TopicRowCuesTests.swift:84-91`.\n   - Scenario: put `.accessibilityLabel(\"Ouvrir le forum\")` back in `TopicListView.swift:220` and keep the helper. The test stays green, so it does not check the bug's wiring (LESSONS 2, \"cannot pass trivially\").\n   - Context: the helper only returns `title`, so the test asserts its own definition. Testing SwiftUI modifiers is not practical in this target, and `topicCountLabel` already uses this helper pattern, so I accept it.\n   - Fix: say so in the PR's \"Tests\" section and add a VoiceOver check to the Mac pass, so nobody reads it as a guard against this regression.\n2. **Detail**, `TopicListView.swift:222`. `.accessibilityAddTraits(.isButton)` repeats a trait a `Button` already has, even with `.plain` style. It does no harm, and the issue asks for it explicitly, so leave it.\n3. **Detail**, `TopicRowCuesTests.swift:91`. The last `#expect` follows from the loop above it and adds nothing. It is optional.\n\n**Vérifié**\n- Read the diff, the whole `header(_:title:)` at dad86ce (the count `Text` and the fold chevron keep their own labels, and no `.combine` merges the header) and the test file header.\n- Searched for other uses of « Ouvrir le forum »: none are left.\n- Read LESSONS line 2.\n- Did not build or run anything: the cloud cannot build the app target, and this diff touches no HFRKit code.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
